# The partitions that run.sh makes with sfdisk on the 64 MiB disk image of devices=esp-disk.
# The EFI system partition has 40 MiB, as busybox mkdosfs makes only FAT32, with 512-byte
# clusters, which the firmware refuses with fewer than 65525 clusters (edk2-stable202608
# FatPkg/EnhancedFatDxe/Init.c FatOpenDevice). It is GPT entry 2 but comes first on the disk, as
# a Hard Drive node numbers a partition by its entry (UEFI 2.11 §10.3.5.1), not by its place.
# src/lib/esp/sfdisk_images.rs holds what sfdisk writes of this script as QEMU_ESP_DISK.
label: gpt
